  "limitations": [
    "Verdict is limited to the approved STEP1 implementation/review-export-render-concrete-preview chain and the narrow new fixes. No blocking actual bug was established. Missing native, cloud, managed apply, GPU/runtime, source reachability or full no-change installation qualification is not treated as STEP1 implementation failure.",
    "Only source text and retained report/log bytes were read; Python stdlib AST/JSON/hash/diff processing was used. No tests, subprocess probes, project imports, managed imports, fixture creation, installer calls, real observation, network, Git, settings/credentials/workstation inspection or repository edits were performed by this reviewer. The only file written is /tmp/isaac-step1-final-review.json.",
    "Current-source hashes identify bytes at review time, not a frozen tree or cryptographically attested historical execution. Comparison against all initial audit fingerprints found changes only in metadata_readers.py, profile_discovery.py, workspace_paths.py and installer_desired_profile.test.py among that original list; the new workspace test and verification scripts were additionally inspected.",
    "Retained /tmp runner/demo copies differ from checked-in verification copies by added spec/loader assertions and demo import profile_parser becoming importlib.import_module(\"profile_parser\"). Those textual differences were reviewed as equivalent successful-path loading, not silently represented as byte-identical test provenance. No new execution of checked-in copies was performed.",
    "Source extent: full narrow helper/desired bridge/profile workflow and runner/demo text; candidate validation/review/rescan/origin sections; new regression methods and related evidence-method boundaries; targeted mapper/parser/output/predispatch and public-flag/template transport sections. Fingerprinting the remaining bytes of these files does not certify every legacy/native/deployment behavior in them. Initial broad audit remains secondary context.",
    "Runner controls are bounded trusted-code verification controls, not a hostile-code/general sandbox certificate. Landlock has explicit trusted repository, /usr and library aliases, selected temp, loader/localtime and /dev/null exceptions; temporary rights include executable fixture seams. Audit hook is a same-interpreter Python guard, not a universal subprocess import restriction. Root-only tests were skipped, not passed.",
    "Demo observation uses synthetic HEAD/config and environment metadata, not a valid fetched Git revision or installed environment. The example archive URL/hash and Git commit do not prove public reachability, authenticity, buildability or native runtime conformance. No managed ownership was fabricated and target metadata stays managed=false.",
    "Non-mutation evidence is specifically the demo assertion comparing fixture regular-file content hashes/modes and checking that the precreated empty target home stays empty. This does not prove all directory metadata, timestamps, ACLs, arbitrary links or an actual workstation remained unchanged. The target-home directory was deliberately created before CLI calls solely for the writer exclusion-root contract; installation_targets_created=false must not be read as no fixture directory creation.",
    "Custom-tool success is mapper and legacy-parser acceptance of an optional exact PyPI dependency using location=null. Required unsupported declarations remain gated; the concrete planner still labels package/runtime execution unqualified. This does not establish package availability, installation, dependency compatibility or playbook/native consumer acceptance.",
    "A concrete dry-run with blocked/unknown/would_change statuses is not a converged all-satisfied workstation. Runtime prefix unknowns, absent Sim changes and blocked existing checkout are correct retained boundaries here. No authorization is inferred for a real workstation scan or any work beyond STEP1.",
    "One targeted search used a nonexistent deployers.py spelling; it returned the existing deployer.py alternative, which was then read. Broad/truncated outputs were followed by targeted reads or JSON processing; no execution fallback was used.",
    "Final update: /tmp/isaac-step1-ptww1ez4 and /tmp/isaac-step1-demo-j0pu_ozq are the primary current acceptance receipts. Earlier RED logs are retained solely for regression causality; the denied initial managed import is retained solely for the guard boundary. No failed intermediate expanded run is presented as the final result. The initially inspected 03lxxwmf demo is superseded by the final j0pu_ozq artifact checks. The parent states there were no production edits since the final run; independent fingerprint comparison found no mismatch among all 39 recorded files. Additional source rows from that manifest are hash-only provenance unless included in the source extents above."
